<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Aesthetics Results.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Aesthetics Results. ‣ 3.2 Experimental Results ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ SlidesGen-Bench: Evaluating Slides Generation via Computational and Quantitative Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, Skywork-Banana outperforms all baseline methods in the aggregate evaluation. Notably, Skywork-Banana achieves the highest scores in the overall Aesthetics Score (27.28 vs. 26.58 for the runner-up) and Engagement (8.30 vs. 6.41), suggesting that Skywork-Banana is particularly effective at generating high-fidelity, visually engaging slides. Models with lower aesthetic scores, such as Gamma and Quark, have a relative flat narrative pace of the generated slides, resulting in significantly lower Rhythm scores. The analysis of the aesthetics results for different presentation purpose is in Appendix <a href="#A10" title="Appendix J Aesthetics results for different purpose ‣ SlidesGen-Bench: Evaluating Slides Generation via Computational and Quantitative Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S3.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Product</span></td>
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Usability</span> (<math id="S3.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Engagement</span> (<math id="S3.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Harmony</span> (<math id="S3.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rhythm</span> (<math id="S3.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S3.T4.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aesthetics</span> (<math id="S3.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
