<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>Parameter Optimization Results</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using 50 human-ranked slide pairs, we performed grid search to maximize Spearman <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (Table <a href="#A5.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ E.6 Parameter Optimization Results ‣ Appendix E Aesthetic Metrics Parameter Tuning ‣ SlidesGen-Bench: Evaluating Slides Generation via Computational and Quantitative Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Parameter Optimization Results</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T13.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><span id="A5.T13.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric</span></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><span id="A5.T13.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Param</span></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><span id="A5.T13.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Init</span></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><span id="A5.T13.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Opt</span></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">ColorHarmony</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">1</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.01</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">+0.08</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">VisualHRV</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.1</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.02</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">+0.05</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">VisualHRV</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.3</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.1</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">+0.03</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">SubbandEntropy</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.84</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.84</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">–</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T13.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T13.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">Colorfulness</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;"><math id="A5.T13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.30</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">0.30</td>
<td id="A5.T13.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.5pt;padding-bottom:-0.5pt;">–</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">SubbandEntropy and Colorfulness parameters retained literature values (<math id="A5.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>). ColorHarmony <math id="A5.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> showed largest sensitivity, with stricter threshold better distinguishing professional designs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.7 </span>Summary</h3>

<div id="A5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our tuning combines principled estimates from empirical distributions with human judgment refinement:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SubbandEntropy</span>: Literature weights (<math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{L}\!=\!0.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{L}\!=\!0.84</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ab}\!=\!0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ab}\!=\!0.08</annotation></semantics></math>) optimal</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Colorfulness</span>: Hasler-Süsstrunk <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> generalizes well</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ColorHarmony</span>: Stricter <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\!=\!0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\!=\!0.01</annotation></semantics></math> captures professional standards</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VisualHRV</span>: <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\!=\!0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\!=\!0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\!=\!0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\!=\!0.75</annotation></semantics></math> balances variety vs. cognitive load</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Layout Detection Examples</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ the PP-DocLayout_plus-L model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cui et al. (2025)</a></cite> to detect and localize textual elements within presentation slides. This deep learning-based layout analysis model provides precise bounding box coordinates for various element types, including document titles, body text, images, and footers. Each detected element is assigned a confidence score indicating the model’s certainty in the detection.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Detection Output Format</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model outputs a structured JSON format containing the following information for each detected element:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">label</span>: The semantic category of the detected region (e.g., <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">text</span>, <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">image</span>, <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">doc_title</span>, <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">footer</span>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">score</span>: Confidence score ranging from 0 to 1, representing the model’s certainty</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">coordinate</span>: Bounding box coordinates in the format <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x_{\min},y_{\min},x_{\max},y_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{\min},y_{\min},x_{\max},y_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Example for OCR Detections</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ F.2 Example for OCR Detections ‣ Appendix F Layout Detection Examples ‣ SlidesGen-Bench: Evaluating Slides Generation via Computational and Quantitative Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> illustrates the layout detection results on representative slides from the <span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Modern Architecture</span> presentation. The detected bounding boxes are visualized with different colors corresponding to element types: titles (green), body text (blue), images (red), and footers (gray).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2601.09487v1/figures/detection/slide_0001_res.png" id="A6.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/212;" width="381" height="212" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Title slide with a full-width background image, document title, subtitle text, and footer.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2601.09487v1/figures/detection/slide_0002_res.png" id="A6.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/212;" width="381" height="212" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Content slide with side-by-side images, title, dual text blocks, and footer.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2601.09487v1/figures/detection/slide_0005_res.png" id="A6.F11.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/212;" width="381" height="212" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Two-column layout with title, multiple text regions, and a large image on the right.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Layout detection results using PP-DocLayout_plus-L on presentation slides. Bounding boxes are color-coded by element type: images, document titles, text, and footers <em id="A6.F11.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">etc.</em>. Confidence scores are displayed alongside each detection.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Detection Statistics</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ F.3 Detection Statistics ‣ Appendix F Layout Detection Examples ‣ SlidesGen-Bench: Evaluating Slides Generation via Computational and Quantitative Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> summarizes the detection results across the example presentation slides. The model demonstrates high accuracy in identifying textual elements, with average confidence scores exceeding 0.90 for text regions and 0.80 for document titles.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Summary of layout detection results on example slides.</figcaption>
